<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The widget frame, with a fixed number of task slots.

  DELIBERATELY DULL. Two previous versions failed on this device: a ListView
  fed by a RemoteViewsService drew "Couldn't add widget." in every row, and
  replacing it with RemoteViews.addView of nested row layouts made the launcher
  reject the whole thing with "Can't load widget".

  So there is no dynamic construction left at all. Every row exists in this
  file, and the provider only ever calls setTextViewText, setViewVisibility,
  setTextColor and setOnClickPendingIntent on ids declared right here. Those
  are the oldest and least exotic RemoteViews operations there are. The cost is
  a fixed maximum of 8 rows and a repetitive file; the benefit is that
  there is no mechanism left that can fail.

  Bars are TextViews rather than plain Views on purpose: TextView is on the
  documented list of widget-supported classes and View is not. It almost
  certainly works either way, but this removes one more unknown.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
